# gamescope, built from source with a checked-in PKGBUILD (`pkgbuild_local` below), not fetched
# from the holo monorepo. build-overlay.sh uses that recipe and applies `patches:` to it; makepkg
# clones the upstream gamescope tag (pkgver in the PKGBUILD, 3.17.0 now) and the submodule commits
# recorded at that tag. Each patch is described in patches/README.md.
#
# Why we own the recipe: holo pinned 3.16.17, whose explicit-sync present path deadlocked on the
# first frame on ~2/3 of cold session starts here, and we build from source for our patches anyway.
# Our first patch, composite rotation when the DPU cannot ROTATE_90 a LINEAR plane, is upstream
# since 3.16.28 (our PR #2228): gamescope turns it on by itself when the plane lacks the rotation.
#
# The series, by area (numbers are not compacted, so old commits still resolve; 0006 is a
# diagnostic kept out of the list):
#   0001          --rotated-output-max-height: a panel wider than the DPU inline rotator's
#                 1088-line cap (Pocket S2) renders at 1080 lines and keeps scanout rotation.
#   0002-0005     night-mode atom, fake output size, FPS-limit atom, Steam focus under
#                 SteamControlled.
#   0007          wayland-protocols wrap for the wlroots 0.20 floor.
#   0014, 0016-0018  colour management on direct scanout through the DPU's CTM and output LUTs.
#   0019-0021     fragment-shader composite (--composite-graphics), libliftoff plane zpos.
#   0025          clock-anchored FPS limiter for fixed-refresh panels.
#   0026-0035     composite blit (--composite-blit): when the plane cannot rotate (SM6115), layers
#                 are turned by a VK_QCOM_rotated_copy blit and scanned out unrotated instead of
#                 composited every frame; 0030 keeps the DPU colour management on a blitted frame,
#                 0032 maps images on a GPU without cached+coherent memory.
#   0033, 0036    touch on SoC touchscreens: rotated with the panel, no cursor on a touch.
#   0040-0046     a second panel driven by the same gamescope (--secondary-output,
#                 --secondary-touch-device), direct scanout first, panel off while unused.
#   0047-0048     refresh rates from an EDID-less panel's native modes; a refresh-only request
#                 takes that exact mode.
#   0049-0050     Steam on another XWayland sees the focus; the boot splash holds until the shell
#                 draws.
#   0054-0056     FIFO queue bound, late input sampling, KMS device closed under the wlserver lock.
#
# Flags that exist only in this gamescope: --rotated-output-max-height (0001),
# --composite-graphics (0019), --composite-blit (0027), --secondary-output and
# --secondary-touch-device (0040, 0043). An unknown argument makes gamescope exit, so dropping one
# of those patches means changing etc/retroforge/session.conf or retroforge-session in the same
# commit. tests/test-session.sh checks 0040, 0043 and 0049 against this list.
#
# 0014 depends on the kernel. Setting a CTM only works because kernel patch 0330 carries 8/10 of
# Dmitry Baryshkov's "drm/msm: fix SMMU fault dumps" v4: without it a colour-management change
# re-reserves DPU resources without reprogramming the encoder, CTL_FLUSH is written as zero and the
# display freezes. If 0330 ever loses that part, 0014 comes out in the same commit.
#
# To bump gamescope: change pkgver in the PKGBUILD, apply the patches to the new tag cumulatively,
# in this order, on a clone with submodules (several build on earlier ones, so a per-patch dry-run
# against a clean tree reports false failures; 0020/0021 patch the libliftoff submodule), and
# re-roll only the ones that fail. Also compare the tag's .gitmodules with the PKGBUILD's source=()
# and its meson_options.txt with the -D flags in build().
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build dir and repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path, relative to this dir, of the checked-in PKGBUILD
#   pkgrel_suffix  appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel (N -> N.<suffix>) so pacman prefers our build
#                  over holo's; an integer (makepkg wants pkgrel = integer[.integer])
#   patches        files under patches/, applied in this order with `patch -p1` in the gamescope
#                  source root (after `cd gamescope` in prepare())
name: gamescope
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-drmbackend-rotated-output-max-height.patch 0002-sanitize-nightmode-atom.patch 0003-drmbackend-fake-output-mm.patch 0004-fps-limit-atom-persist.patch 0005-steamcontrolled-steam-focus-fallback.patch 0007-vendor-wayland-protocols-wrap.patch 0014-drm-color-manage-direct-scanout-via-the-dpu-ctm.patch 0016-steamcompmgr-arm64-virtual-white.patch 0017-color-neutral-virtual-white-keeps-scanout.patch 0018-drm-sdr-color-management-through-the-dpu-output-luts.patch 0019-rendervulkan-fragment-shader-composite.patch 0020-libliftoff-treat-enodev-as-no-fit.patch 0021-libliftoff-give-planes-the-layer-zpos.patch 0025-steamcompmgr-elapsed-time-fps-limiter.patch 0026-rendervulkan-upscale-cache-compressed.patch 0027-rendervulkan-composite-blit-rotated-copy.patch 0028-drmbackend-pre-rotate-layers-the-plane-cannot-rotate.patch 0029-rendervulkan-safe-compute-fallback.patch 0030-composite-blit-keeps-the-dpu-colour-management.patch 0031-composite-blit-build-under-werror-format-security.patch 0032-rendervulkan-mappable-image-without-cached-coherent-memory.patch 0033-wlserver-rotate-touch-on-spi-and-soc-touchscreens.patch 0034-composite-blit-keep-the-rotated-copy-of-an-unchanged-layer.patch 0035-scan-out-a-client-pre-rotated-buffer-unrotated.patch 0036-wlserver-touch-does-not-show-the-cursor.patch 0040-drm-drive-a-secondary-output.patch 0041-steamcompmgr-route-second-screen-windows-to-the-secondary-output.patch 0042-paint-the-secondary-output-direct-scanout-first.patch 0043-wlserver-route-the-secondary-touchscreen-to-the-secondary-output.patch 0044-secondary-output-direct-scanout-rotated-on-the-plane.patch 0045-xwayland-the-secondary-output-gets-its-own-area-of-the-x-screen.patch 0046-secondary-output-panel-off-while-nothing-is-shown-there.patch 0047-drm-offer-an-edid-less-internal-panels-native-modes-as-refresh-rates.patch 0048-steamcompmgr-refresh-only-request-takes-the-exact-mode.patch 0049-steamcompmgr-steam-on-another-xwayland-sees-the-focus.patch 0050-steamcompmgr-hold-the-boot-splash-until-the-shell-draws.patch 0054-layer-bound-the-fifo-queue.patch 0055-layer-late-input-sampling.patch 0056-wlserver-close-the-kms-device-under-the-wlserver-lock.patch
